[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115169,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondrodermatitis nodularis chronica helicis (CNCH) is a non-neoplastic, inflammatory, degenerative process of the external ear, characterized by necrobiotic changes in the dermis and perichondrium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115170,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115171,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AA12 Chondrodermatitis nodularis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115172,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> chondrodermatitis nodularis helicis.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Winkler disease; chondrodermatitis chronica auriculae.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115173,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115174,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The helix is affected twice as often as the antihelix, but any part of the auricle may be affected {17524165; 27399947}, with the right affected more than the left {13079290; 13124280; 21276202; 24206803}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115175,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present clinically with an intensely painful nodule. The pain is usually nocturnal and magnified by any ear pressure {13079290; 13124280; 21276202; 24206803; 30505787}. CNCH begins as a reddish, round, indurated nodule, which develops a central crater containing crust-like to horny material, with atrophic adjacent skin. Drainage of purulent material is common. Dermoscopy shows a global configuration (daisy pattern) of thick white lines, radially arranged and converging on a central rounded lump {29926164; 30775149}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115176,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p>CNCH is a relatively common external ear skin lesion {13079290; 17524165; 27399947} with a male predilection (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 2:1) {17524165; 21276202; 24206803; 27399947}. Most patients are in their seventh decade of life {13079290; 17524165; 21276202; 24206803; 27399947}. Young patients may have an underlying systemic disease causing ischaemic necrobiosis {15811116}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-24T15:06:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115177,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Exposure to sunlight or cold predisposes individuals to CNCH {24206803}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115178,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dermal microtrauma (e.g. due to helmets, headsets, actinic damage, frostbite) combined with the relatively tenuous aural vascularity {19413613; 29805936} leads to subepidermal injury, and with reduced repair capacity and collagen degeneration in the elderly, the lesion becomes persistent {13079290; 15811116}. Systemic diseases associated with microangiopathy may predispose individuals to CNCH {13079290; 15811116; 21276202}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115179,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CNCH appears as a small central crater, usually 4&ndash;15&nbsp;mm, containing necrotic material.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115180,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A central cup-shaped crater is filled with necrotic debris, fibrin, and a variable number of inflammatory cells. A parakeratotic and hyperkeratotic crust is usually present, surrounded by acanthotic epithelium often with acute inflammation. An inverted funnel&ndash;shaped defect is present in the dermis, with the collagen underlying the crater appearing homogeneous and eosinophilic, admixed with fibrin. There is superficial cartilage erosion with loss of cartilage basophilia, associated with fibrosis and chondrocyte dropout causing smudgy cartilage degeneration. Rarely, devitalized cartilage may extrude through the crater.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>CNCH is very commonly confused clinically with skin neoplasms (squamous or basal cell carcinoma), and rarely with relapsing polychondritis or granuloma annulare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115181,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115182,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115183,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a cup-shaped crater with necrotic debris and fibrin extending to involve the superficial cartilage.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115184,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115185,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 348,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrences occur in as many as 35% of patients and usually develop within a year {15149500; 19116517; 24684884; 27399947}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:13:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
